body:
SC legislature has repeatedly engaged in theocratic governance. See e.g.

Mandatory posting  of 10 Commandments in schools;

Limiting abortion such that by the time women find out they are actually pregnant, it is not available; limit/criminalizing medications for abortion or abortions themselves;

Discriminatory taxation rules against LGTBQ married couples;

School vouchers that divert state tax dollars to religious schools;

I've been a Christian my ENTIRE LIFE.  I am male &amp; straight. But EACH is an attempt to LEGISLATE religious beliefs, &amp; IT HAS TO STOP.
